CRASH INVESTIGATION 2026-10-28 (attribution OPEN — do not treat as settled)

  Two crashes while testing today (ReportQueue 16:04:38 + 16:13:45, both
  EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION reading 0xD0). Both minidumps walked (utils/dmpwalk.py --disasm,
  plus raw memory reads off the dump):

  MECHANISM (settled): a virtual call through vtable slot 0xD0 on an object whose vtable
    pointer is ZERO — the object memory is already FREED (dump 1: block fully zeroed; dump 2:
    +0 zeroed like a freelist marker, rest repurposed). Up-stack is a nested deleting-
    destructor cascade (MI engine object, vtables at +0/+0x160, members at +0x3a8 -> +0x10/+0
    -> +0x98) releasing member handles through HandleSharedStorage::ReleaseWeak (named in
    cyberpunk2077_addresses.json). I.e. use-after-free / double-release of a shared engine
    handle during object-graph teardown. Main thread, mid-gameplay (telemetry: IsClosing=false,
    LoadingStage=Finished, mounted, Badlands; uptime 471 s / 502 s). Both crashes identical:
    same RIP (exe+0xb0c78a), same registers (rbp=-1, r9=0xff, r10=4), same container layout.

  ATTRIBUTION (OPEN): CrashReporter.log shows THREE earlier crashes — 10/26 20:40 (game 2.31)
    and 10/27 02:10 + 04:24 (game 2.5) — BEFORE this mod was ever installed (first plugin log
    is 15:47 on 10/28). Their dumps were cleaned up, so those signatures cannot be compared.
    The game crashes on this install WITHOUT this mod. Counter-evidence: both of today's
    crashes are in mod+harness sessions; the plugin's native surface has no frames anywhere in
    the stack scan and holds no engine handles (all native params scalar, probe runs through
    RTTI on raw pointers). Candidates: (a) harness/CET entity-handle lifetime (M.avEntity held
    across despawn; CET is v1.38.1 [HEAD], a dev build), (b) the plugin, (c) a 2.5-era base or
    CET bug. Do NOT record a culprit before the one-variable retest.

  FIXED WHILE HERE: harness col() used ToColor{}, which CET 1.38 (game 2.5) no longer provides.
    Every Draw() with a live path threw a Lua error EVERY FRAME (~12k errors/min, two 5 MB log
    rotations in one session) and the debug drawing never drew at all. Now probes
    ToColor{} -> Color.new{...} -> Color.new(...) once and skips drawing quietly if none work.
    The flood is gone as a variable for the retest.

  RETEST PLAN (one variable at a time, same ~8 min play pattern — two crashes hit at 7m32s and
  8m03s):
    A. mod + harness (as deployed now, with the ToColor fix)
    B. DLL + reds only — rename mods/VNavTest/init.lua aside
    C. whole mod removed
  If a crash occurs, run `python utils/dmpwalk.py --disasm`: same RIP exe+0xb0c78a = same bug.
  KEEP the ReportQueue folder afterwards — the report cleaner deletes old ones, and those
  dumps being gone is the only reason the 10/27 crashes can't be compared.

STATUS 2026-10-28 — GAME PATCH 2.5 MIGRATION (2.31 -> 2.5, game patched 2026-10-27).

  The mod was last built 2026-10-14 against a pre-2.5 RED4ext.SDK and would NOT have loaded
  cleanly on 2.5: the patch changed the engine ABI the plugin is compiled against —
  CBaseFunction 0xB0 -> 0xF0, CStackFrame 0x68 -> 0xA8, CGameEngine::framework 0x308 -> 0x348,
  IRTTISystem gained 4 virtuals, SDK address hashes re-pointed, and
  RED4EXT_V1_RUNTIME_VERSION_LATEST now targets 2.50 (RED4ext checks it at load).

  DONE  re-pinned vendor/RED4ext.SDK to upstream 5246e65 ("Update types for patch 2.5 (#232)").
        No source changes were needed - the SDK update was ABI-internal.
  DONE  rebuilt all targets (VS 2026 / CMake 4.4.4; the old build/ was a stale cross-machine
        CMake cache and was regenerated). 3017 offline checks green.
  DONE  verified the probe ABI against the 2.5 decompile (codeberg PR #32, head 17c62d00):
        TraceResult unchanged ({position, normal, material} - fits the 0x60 buffer),
        OverlapByQueryFilter still 5 params in order, QueryFilter.AddGroup unchanged,
        and Overlap's queryPreset overload lives on StateGameScriptInterface, so
        GetFunction("Overlap") on the queries system stays unambiguous.
  DONE  verified every game API the .reds use against 2.5 (GetTargetParts, TSQ_ALL,
        TargetSearchQuery, TS_TargetPartInfo.GetComponent, IComponent.GetEntity,
        Entity.GetEntityID/GetWorldPosition, IsPathIntersectingWithTraffic,
        GetTargetingSystem/GetTrafficSystem/GetDelaySystem, DelayCallbackNextFrame) -
        all present, signatures unchanged. scc headless compile gate passes on both files.
        (COMPILE GATE ONLY - not verification; only a game launch verifies.)
  DONE  verified the CET harness's Codeware surface against THIS install's compiled blob
        (final.redscripts.modded): DynamicEntitySpec / GetDynamicEntitySystem / spawnInView /
        alwaysSpawned / persistSpawn all present on Codeware 1.21.1 + game 2.5.
  DONE  nightcity.vnavbake RE-EXTRACTED from the 2.5 archives (WolvenKit navbake) and
        re-voxelised with --gamebuild 2.5, so V2's stamp check is live (was: unstamped).
        VNavTest now attaches via VNavAttachBakeChecked with expected build "2.5" by default.
  DONE  old-vs-new geometry question MEASURED with `vnav_bake --compare` (2.3 bake vs 2.5 bake,
        1 m voxels): 508,112,069 solid voxels in both (100.0% of each), 4,012 only in 2.3,
        59,001 only in 2.5. World geometry effectively unchanged between those patches - the
        shipped bake is re-extracted anyway, so that is measured, not assumed.
  DONE  vnav_bake usage text now documents --gamebuild (it existed but was undocumented).
  FOUND the --gamebuild flag was parsed and then DROPPED - BakedNavWriter::SetGameBuild was
        called from tests only, never from vnav_bake's main. A bake "re-baked with --gamebuild"
        would have come out UNSTAMPED anyway while looking stamped. Fixed (wired + the summary
        now echoes the stamp, and warns when there is none); --inspect confirms "game build: 2.5"
        round-trips through the loader the game uses. Lesson: verify the artifact, not the flag.
  NOTE  this deploy builds with -DVNAV_LOGGING=ON on purpose (test run). Rebuild with logging
        OFF before shipping anything.

