FOUND WHILE DOING THE ABOVE (not on either list):
  DONE  probe budget over-blocked narrow space. maxProbesPerChunk was 2048; full refinement of a
        16^3 chunk costs ~4681 probes (up to 8777 with the leaf hard-inflation probe), so anything
        needing leaf detail everywhere resolved to SOLID. Measured: a 4 m corridor read as
        completely filled in (every query Unreachable) at 2048 and is passable at 9216, which is
        now the default. maxProbesPerQuery raised to 276480 to keep the documented ~30-chunk
        reach. Pinned by TestProbeBudgetOverBlocking.

DYNAMIC OBSTACLES — producer shipped 2026-08-16 (code/r6/scripts/PathfindingUpdate/DynamicObstacles.reds)

  L5 shipped the dynamic obstacle LAYER but nothing fed it: 3 native declarations, 0 callers, so the
  planner still routed straight through traffic. That producer now exists.

  HARD CONSTRAINT, checked not assumed: the producer MUST work at entity level.
    - TraceResult is { position, normal, material } — NO entity handle. A physics overlap can say
      something is there but never what, and gives no extents to build an AABB from.
    - And probe results feed the CACHED chunk grid, which is exactly what the separate layer exists
      to avoid poisoning.
    So "add Vehicle to the collision mask" is not a route to this, on two independent grounds.

  TRAP: TrafficSystem.FindEntitiesNearPlane(... entityIDs: [wref<Entity>]) looks perfect and is
  UNUSABLE from redscript — that output array is not marked `out`, and redscript arrays are value
  types, so nothing comes back. Do not spend time on it again.

  Two tiers, complementary:
    Tier 1  VNavDynamic.Refresh(volume, instigator, radius)  — PREVENTIVE. TargetingSystem
            .GetTargetParts (proper `out` array) -> dedupe by EntityID -> VNavDynamicAdd. Makes the
            SEARCH route around obstacles. ~0.2 s cadence is ample; the search pins the snapshot.
    Tier 2  VNavDynamic.PathHitsTraffic(gi, path, clearance, out hit) — REACTIVE. Vanilla's
            TrafficSystem.IsPathIntersectingWithTraffic, which takes exactly the shape
            VNav.GetPoints() returns. Nearly free; catches what moved since the last Refresh, but
            can only reject a path, never route around.

  Every API in that file was verified against cyberpunkDecompiledScripts before writing. Two were
  wrong on first look and got corrected: GetWorldPosition/GetEntityID at orphans.swift:37455/37465
  are IMappin's, not Entity's — the real ones are core/entity/entity.swift:44 and :8.

  ⚠ UNTESTED. Redscript cannot be typechecked without launching the game. Also: GetTargetParts
  enumerates what the TARGETING system considers a target, which covers live NPCs and traffic but
  may miss empty parked cars — pair Tier 1 with Tier 2 rather than trusting the snapshot alone.

